    body: `{{effectiveDate}}

{{employee}}{{#if employeeAddress}}
{{employeeAddress}}{{/if}}

Dear {{employee}},

{{employer}} is pleased to offer you the position of {{position}}{{#if supervisor}}, reporting to {{supervisor}}{{/if}}, starting {{startDate}}{{#if location}} at {{location}}{{/if}}.

PAY
You will be paid {{#if payType=hourly}}{{rate}} per hour{{else}}a salary of {{rate}} per year{{/if}}, {{#if payFrequency=weekly}}every week{{/if}}{{#if payFrequency=biweekly}}every two weeks{{/if}}{{#if payFrequency=semimonthly}}twice each month{{/if}}{{#if payFrequency=monthly}}once a month{{/if}}, on {{employer}}'s regular paydays{{#if payday}} ({{payday}}){{/if}}, less required tax withholding and any deductions you authorize in writing. {{employer}} will give you at least one pay period's notice before it changes your payday or lowers your rate of pay, and will give you a pay statement each pay period.{{#if schedule}} Your expected schedule is {{schedule}}.{{/if}} {{#if payType=hourly}}Hours over 40 in a workweek are paid at overtime rates as the law requires.{{else}}A salary alone does not make a position exempt from overtime. Unless {{employer}} tells you in writing that your position is exempt, you will be paid overtime for hours over 40 in a workweek as the law requires.{{/if}}
{{#if benefits}}
BENEFITS AND OTHER TERMS
{{benefits}}
{{/if}}
LEAVE
Earned sick and safe leave. Under the Maryland Healthy Working Families Act, you will earn {{#if sickLeave=paid}}paid{{else}}unpaid{{/if}} sick and safe leave at the rate of at least 1 hour for every 30 hours you work. {{employer}} need not let you earn or carry over more than 40 hours a year, use more than 64 hours a year, or use the leave during your first 106 calendar days of work. You may use it for your own or a family member's illness, injury, condition or preventive care; for maternity or paternity leave; and when you are absent because of domestic violence, sexual assault or stalking committed against you or a family member. {{employer}} will not discharge, demote, threaten or take any other adverse action against you for using this leave in good faith. If you believe your rights under the Act have been violated, you may report it to the Commissioner of Labor and Industry or bring a civil action as the Act allows. Unused earned sick and safe leave is not paid out when employment ends (if you are rehired within 37 weeks, your unused balance is restored), and the Act does not cover employees who regularly work fewer than 12 hours a week. {{employer}} will show you your available balance whenever you are paid and will give you the State's written notice about this leave. Any vacation or other paid leave, and whether unused leave other than earned sick and safe leave is paid when employment ends, is stated above or in {{employer}}'s written leave policy.

AT-WILL EMPLOYMENT
Your employment is at will. Either you or {{employer}} may end it at any time, with or without cause or notice. This letter is not a contract for any fixed period. Only an owner or officer of {{employer}} can change this at-will relationship, and only in a signed writing. This letter replaces any earlier oral statements about your job.

BEFORE YOU START
By your first day, please give {{employer}} a completed federal Form W-4 and Maryland Form MW507 (both for tax withholding) and complete Section 1 of Form I-9. If you do not return the tax forms, tax will be withheld as the law provides for an employee who has not filed them. Within three business days after you start (or on your first day, if the job lasts less than three business days), you must show {{employer}} original documents of your own choice, from the Form I-9 lists of acceptable documents, proving your identity and your authorization to work in the United States; {{employer}} cannot tell you which documents to show. Your employment depends on completing Form I-9 as federal law requires. As the law requires, {{employer}} will report your hiring to the Maryland new-hire registry within 20 days after you start; the report includes your name, address, Social Security number, start date and starting wage.

This letter is governed by the laws of the State of {{state}}. To accept, sign below and return it by {{replyBy}}; this offer ends if it is not accepted by then.

Sincerely,
{{employer}}
Printed name and title: ______________________________
Signature: ______________________________   Date: ______________

I accept this offer:
{{employee}}
Signature: ______________________________   Date: ______________`,
