    body: `{{effectiveDate}}

{{employee}}{{#if employeeAddress}}
{{employeeAddress}}{{/if}}

Re: End of employment

Dear {{employee}},

{{#if type=resignation}}This letter confirms that {{employer}} has accepted your resignation. Your last day of work is {{lastDay}}.{{/if}}{{#if type=termination}}This letter confirms that your employment with {{employer}} ends on {{lastDay}}.{{/if}}{{#if type=layoff}}This letter confirms that your position with {{employer}} is being eliminated and your last day of work is {{lastDay}}.{{/if}}{{#if reason}}{{#if !type=termination}} {{reason}}{{/if}}{{/if}}

FINAL PAY
Your final paycheck, covering all wages earned through {{lastDay}}{{#if accruedPay}} and unused paid time off{{/if}}, less required withholdings, will be paid on or before {{finalPayDate}}, which is no later than the regular payday that would have applied had your employment continued.{{#if !accruedPay}} Unused vacation or paid time off is handled as {{employer}}'s written leave policy provides and as the law requires. Unused earned sick and safe leave is not paid out when employment ends; if {{employer}} rehires you within 37 weeks, your unused balance will be restored.{{/if}}

{{#if property}}COMPANY PROPERTY
Please return the following promptly, and no later than your last day if that day has not yet passed: {{#if propertyList}}{{propertyList}}{{else}}all company property in your possession{{/if}}. {{employer}} will not deduct the value of anything not returned from your pay unless you have authorized the deduction in writing or the law allows it.

{{/if}}{{#if healthPlan}}HEALTH COVERAGE
Your coverage under {{employer}}'s group health plan ends as the plan's terms provide. You may have the right to continue the coverage, at your own cost, for up to 18 months under Maryland law (Insurance Article §15-409) if the plan is an insured group plan, you live in Maryland, you have been covered for at least 3 months and your employment did not end for cause. You pay the full cost of the coverage plus a reasonable administrative fee. To choose it, you must return a signed election form within the election period, which lasts at least 45 days after your last day; your spouse and dependent children who were covered may be included. If {{employer}} normally had 20 or more employees, the federal COBRA law may also apply to you. {{employer}} will send you the election form within 14 days after you ask for it{{#if contact}} (contact {{contact}}){{/if}}, and you will receive separate written information about your rights under the plan.

{{/if}}UNEMPLOYMENT INSURANCE
You may be able to apply for unemployment insurance benefits with the Maryland Department of Labor (labor.maryland.gov). It is best to apply as soon as your work stops or your hours are reduced. The State decides eligibility. If the State asks {{employer}} about the end of your employment, {{employer}} will answer accurately and on time.

TAX FORMS AND RECORDS
Your Form W-2 will be sent to the address we have on file, so please keep it up to date with us.{{#if contact}} Questions can be sent to {{contact}}.{{/if}}

Sincerely,
{{employer}}
Printed name and title: ______________________________
By: ______________________________   Date: ______________

Received by employee (receipt only, not agreement):
{{employee}}
Signature: ______________________________   Date: ______________
If the employee declined to sign: declined on ______________ in the presence of ______________________`,
