    description: "Confirms that a person works (or worked) for the business — for a landlord, lender or agency.",
    reviewNote: "CHECK THESE FIRST. (1) Get the employee's written request or permission before sending, and keep it. (2) Facts only: no reason for leaving, discipline, medical, immigration or family information, and never a Social Security number or date of birth. (3) Include pay only if the employee asked for it, and say whether it is before or after taxes. DETAIL FOLLOWS. Release employment or pay information only with the employee's written request or permission, and keep a copy of that request. State facts only — never the reason for leaving, discipline, medical, immigration or family information, and never a Social Security number or date of birth. Include pay only if the employee asked for it, and say clearly whether it is before or after taxes. The letter says it is not a promise of continued employment, so a lender does not read it as one. If a lender sends its own form or asks for more, answer only what the employee has allowed.",
