    body: `PROMISSORY NOTE

Date: {{effectiveDate}}
Principal: {{principal}}

1. PROMISE TO PAY
For value received, {{borrower}}{{#if borrowerAddress}} of {{borrowerAddress}}{{/if}} ("Borrower") promises to pay {{lender}}{{#if lenderAddress}} of {{lenderAddress}}{{/if}} ("Lender") {{principal}}{{#if rate}}, with simple interest at {{rate}}% per year (365-day year) on the unpaid balance{{else}}, without interest{{/if}}. Interest and fees together will never exceed the maximum the law allows; any excess is applied to principal or refunded to Borrower. Lender elects, under Commercial Law §12-101.1, that Title 12, Subtitle 1 of the Commercial Law Article governs this loan.

2. PAYMENTS
{{#if schedule=monthly}}Borrower will pay {{months}} monthly installments of {{paymentAmount}} each, on the same day of each month beginning {{firstPayment}}, and will pay all remaining principal{{#if rate}} and interest{{/if}} on {{dueDate}} (the "Maturity Date").{{else}}Borrower will pay the full principal{{#if rate}} and accrued interest{{/if}} in one payment on {{dueDate}} (the "Maturity Date").{{/if}} Payments are made by check or bank transfer to Lender{{#if lenderAddress}} at {{lenderAddress}}{{/if}}, or as Lender later directs in writing. If a due date falls on a Saturday, Sunday or legal holiday, the payment is due on the next business day. Each payment is applied first to costs and late fees, then {{#if rate}}to interest, then {{/if}}to principal.

{{#if financeCharge}}3. LOAN STATEMENT
Lender gave Borrower this statement before Borrower signed (Commercial Law §12-106). Amount borrowed: {{principal}}. Annual effective rate of simple interest: {{rate}}%. Total finance charge over the full term: {{financeCharge}}. Other payments owed to Lender in addition to interest when the loan is made: none.

{{/if}}4. LATE PAYMENT AND DEFAULT
{{#if schedule=monthly}}{{#if lateFee}}If a monthly payment is received more than 15 days after its due date, Borrower will pay a one-time late fee of {{lateFeeAmount}} for that payment, but never more than the law allows. {{/if}}{{/if}}Each of the following is a default: (a) a payment is not made within 10 days after Lender gives written notice that it is past due; (b) the whole balance is not paid on the Maturity Date; (c) Borrower becomes insolvent or files for bankruptcy; {{#if secured}}(d) Borrower gives Lender false information in connection with this note; or (e) the collateral is lost, damaged beyond use, or transferred without Lender's written consent.{{else}}or (d) Borrower gives Lender false information in connection with this note.{{/if}} On default, Lender may declare the whole unpaid balance due immediately by written notice to Borrower.

4. PREPAYMENT
{{#if prepay}}Borrower may pay all or part of the balance early at any time without penalty.{{else}}Early payment requires Lender's written consent.{{/if}}

{{#if secured}}5. SECURITY
To secure this note, Borrower grants Lender a security interest in: {{collateral}}, and authorizes Lender to file financing statements. Borrower will keep the collateral in good repair, insured against loss where that is reasonable, and free of other liens, and will not sell or move it without Lender's written consent. A mortgage or deed of trust on real property needs a separate recorded document, and a lien on a titled vehicle or boat must be noted on its title. The collateral does not include household goods (clothing, furniture, appliances, one radio and one television, linens, china, kitchenware and personal effects) of an individual Borrower or the Borrower's dependents, unless they were bought with this loan. If Borrower defaults, Lender may exercise the rights the law gives a secured lender.

{{/if}}6. COSTS AND GENERAL TERMS
If Borrower defaults, Borrower pays Lender's court costs and other reasonable costs of collection, including attorney's fees actually incurred (not a percentage of the balance) if the debt is sent to an attorney who is not Lender's salaried employee, to the extent the law allows. Borrower waives presentment, demand and protest. If more than one person signs as Borrower, each is responsible for the whole debt. Notices must be in writing and sent to the parties' addresses in this note or to a new address given in writing. Delay or leniency by Lender is not a waiver of any right. Lender may transfer this note; Borrower may not transfer this note or Borrower's duties under it without Lender's written consent. This note binds Borrower's heirs, estate and successors. If any term cannot be enforced, the rest stays in force. This note may be changed only in writing signed by both parties and is governed by the laws of the State of {{state}}.{{#if underSeal}} Borrower signs this note under seal, intending it to be a sealed instrument, and the mark "(SEAL)" next to Borrower's signature is Borrower's seal.{{/if}}

{{#if extraClauses}}7. ADDITIONAL TERMS
{{extraClauses}}

{{/if}}BORROWER: {{borrower}}
Signature{{#if underSeal}} (SEAL){{/if}}: ______________________________   Date: ______________
Printed name: ______________________   Title (if a company): ______________

LENDER: {{lender}}
Signature: ______________________________   Date: ______________
Printed name: ______________________   Title (if a company): ______________`,
