    key: "nda_mutual", title: "Mutual Non-Disclosure Agreement", category: LENDING,
    description: "Two parties agree to keep each other's confidential information private.",
    reviewNote: "CHECK FIRST (3 things): (1) The purpose line must describe the real reason for sharing, because use for any other purpose is a breach. (2) Do NOT use this form to let someone see a client's tax return information: that needs the client's own signed consent (IRC 7216). (3) Pick a confidentiality period that fits (3 years is the default); trade secrets stay protected as long as they stay secret. Keep the protected-disclosures paragraph: federal law requires it in agreements with individuals. DETAIL FOLLOWS. Choose a confidentiality period that fits the information. Trade secrets stay protected as long as they remain secret: under the Maryland Uniform Trade Secrets Act a trade secret is information that has independent economic value from not being generally known and is the subject of reasonable efforts to keep it secret (Commercial Law §11-1201(e)). A court can stop actual or threatened misappropriation (§11-1202) and award damages, and up to twice that for willful and malicious misappropriation (§11-1203); a suit must be brought within 3 years after the misappropriation is, or should have been, discovered (§11-1206). The Act itself awards attorney's fees only for bad faith or willful and malicious misappropriation (§11-1204) but leaves contract remedies untouched (§11-1207(b)), which is why this form has its own fee clause. The whistleblower notice in 18 U.S.C. §1833(b) is included because the federal act requires an employer to give it in any contract with an employee — which includes an individual contractor or consultant — that governs the use of trade secrets or other confidential information; without it the employer cannot recover exemplary damages or attorney's fees in a federal trade-secret case against that individual. Do not delete it. This form has no \"residual knowledge\" clause (letting people use what they remember) — add one only if you decide you want it. It is not a non-compete, and it cannot stop anyone from reporting a suspected legal violation to the government. Client tax-return information cannot be shared under this form: it needs the client's own signed consent (IRC §7216), so use the Authorization to Release Information form for that. Check that the purpose describes the real reason for sharing, because information used for any other purpose is a breach.",
