    body: `COMMERCIAL LEASE

This Lease is made on {{effectiveDate}} between {{landlord}}, {{landlordAddress}} ("Landlord") and {{tenant}}, {{tenantAddress}} ("Tenant").

1. PREMISES AND USE
Landlord leases to Tenant the space at {{premises}} (the "Premises"). Tenant will use it only for {{use}} and in compliance with all laws and required licenses. Landlord does not promise that zoning or any law allows Tenant's use; Tenant is responsible for confirming this and for every license and permit its business needs. Landlord states that it owns the building or has the right to lease the Premises, and Tenant has the quiet use of the Premises as long as Tenant pays the rent and keeps its other promises.

2. TERM
The Lease runs from {{startDate}} to {{endDate}}.{{#if renewal}} Renewal: {{renewalTerms}}.{{/if}} If Landlord wants Tenant to give back the space on the end date, Landlord will give Tenant written notice at least 60 days before the end date (Real Property Article 8-402); if Tenant does not plan to renew or stay, Tenant will give Landlord written notice at least 30 days before it. If Tenant stays with Landlord's written consent, the tenancy continues month to month on the same terms; Landlord may end it on 60 days' written notice and Tenant on 30 days' written notice. If the first term or any renewal term is longer than seven years (Real Property Article 3-101), the parties will sign, within 15 days after the Lease is signed, a memorandum of lease that either of them may record; it states the parties and their addresses, this Lease and its date, the space{{#if legalDescription}} (the land is described as: {{legalDescription}}){{/if}}, the dates of the term and any renewal right with its longest period and exercise dates. Either party may ask the other at any time to sign a memorandum.

3. RENT
Tenant pays {{rent}} per month, due on day {{rentDay}} of each month. Rent not received within {{graceDays}} days after the due date is late{{#if lateFee}} and subject to a late fee of {{lateFeeAmount}}{{/if}}.{{#if nsfFee}} Tenant also pays {{nsfFee}} (never more than $35) for each payment its bank returns unpaid.{{/if}}

4. SECURITY DEPOSIT
Tenant pays a security deposit of {{deposit}}, held by Landlord and returned within 45 days after the Lease ends and Tenant has surrendered the Premises, less amounts needed for unpaid rent or damage beyond normal wear.

5. TAXES AND BUILDING INSURANCE
{{#if taxesBy=landlord}}Landlord pays the property taxes and the insurance on the building.{{else}}Tenant pays the property taxes and the insurance on the building (or, if the building has other tenants, Tenant's fair share by floor area), or repays Landlord for them within 30 days after Landlord's written request with a copy of the bills.{{/if}}

6. UTILITIES
{{#if utilities=tenant}}Tenant pays all utilities for the Premises.{{/if}}{{#if utilities=landlord}}Landlord pays all utilities for the Premises.{{/if}}{{#if utilities=split}}{{utilitiesNote}}{{/if}}

7. MAINTENANCE AND ALTERATIONS
Tenant keeps the Premises clean and in good condition and may not make structural changes without Landlord's written consent. Landlord is responsible for the roof, structure and building systems unless damage is caused by Tenant. Landlord may enter the Premises at reasonable times on reasonable notice to inspect or repair, and at any time in an emergency.

8. INSURANCE AND LIABILITY
Tenant carries commercial general liability insurance of at least {{liabilityAmount}} per occurrence, naming Landlord as an additional insured, plus insurance on its own property. Tenant protects Landlord from claims arising from Tenant's use of the Premises, except those caused by Landlord's negligence.

9. DAMAGE
If the Premises are damaged and cannot be used, rent is reduced until they are repaired. If repairs would take more than 120 days, either party may end the Lease by written notice.

10. DEFAULT
If Tenant does not pay rent within 10 days after written notice, or breaks another term and does not fix it within 30 days after written notice, Landlord may end the Lease, retake possession only through the courts, by the procedures the law provides, and recover what the law allows. Landlord will not lock Tenant out, shut off utilities, or seize, remove or sell Tenant's property to collect rent or retake possession.

11. ASSIGNMENT
Tenant may not assign this Lease or sublet without Landlord's written consent, which will not be unreasonably withheld.

12. END OF LEASE AND HOLDING OVER
At the end of the Lease Tenant returns the Premises clean and in good condition, normal wear excepted. If Tenant stays after the end date without a new written lease, Tenant is a holdover tenant and this is not a renewal: rent is 150% of the last monthly rent, prorated by day, Tenant owes Landlord's resulting damages (never less than the rent under this Lease for the holdover period), and Landlord may recover possession through the courts. Landlord's acceptance of money after the end date or after a notice does not renew the Lease or waive any notice unless the parties agree in writing.

{{#if guarantee}}13. GUARANTEE
{{guarantor}} personally and unconditionally guarantees that Tenant will pay all rent and perform all obligations under this Lease, as amended or renewed, and signs below to confirm it. The guarantee continues despite any change to the Lease or any delay by Landlord, and Landlord need not first pursue Tenant.

{{/if}}{{#if extraClauses}}14. ADDITIONAL TERMS
{{extraClauses}}

{{/if}}15. GENERAL
This is the parties' entire agreement, may be changed only in writing signed by both, binds their successors and permitted assigns, and is governed by the laws of the State of {{state}}. If Landlord sells the building, this Lease continues with the new owner. Notices must be in writing and delivered to the addresses above. If any part is not enforceable, the rest remains in effect. This Lease may be signed in counterparts, including electronically. Each person who signs for a company states that he or she is authorized to do so.

LANDLORD: {{landlord}}
Signature: ______________________________   Date: ______________
If a company — By: ______________________________   Name: ______________________________   Title: ______________________________

TENANT: {{tenant}}
Signature: ______________________________   Date: ______________
If a company — By: ______________________________   Name: ______________________________   Title: ______________________________
{{#if guarantee}}
GUARANTOR: {{guarantor}}
Signature: ______________________________   Date: ______________
{{/if}}`,
