    body: `CONSULTING AGREEMENT

This Agreement is made on {{effectiveDate}} between {{client}}{{#if clientAddress}}, {{clientAddress}}{{/if}} ("Company") and {{consultant}}{{#if consultantAddress}}, {{consultantAddress}}{{/if}} ("Consultant").

1. SERVICES
Consultant will provide the following consulting services: {{scope}} Company will give Consultant, on time, the information, access and decisions Consultant reasonably needs. Any change to the services must be agreed in writing.

2. TERM
Services begin {{startDate}}{{#if hasEnd}} and end {{endDate}}{{else}} and continue until either party gives 30 days' written notice{{/if}}.

3. FEES
Company will pay Consultant {{#if feeType=fixed}}a fixed fee of {{fee}}{{#if feeSchedule}}, invoiced {{feeSchedule}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{#if feeType=hourly}}{{fee}} per hour{{/if}}{{#if feeType=monthly}}{{fee}} per month{{/if}}, payable within {{payDays|day}} of each invoice.{{#if feeType=hourly}} Invoices will show the hours worked.{{/if}}{{#if expenses}} Company reimburses reasonable expenses it approves in advance and that Consultant documents.{{/if}} If Company disputes part of an invoice in good faith, it will tell Consultant in writing before the due date and pay the undisputed part on time.{{#if lateRate}} Amounts unpaid after the due date bear simple interest (not compounded) at {{lateRate}}% per month on the unpaid invoiced amount only, but never more than the maximum rate the law allows.{{/if}}

4. INDEPENDENT CONSULTANT
Consultant is an independent contractor and not Company's employee or partner, controls how and when the work is done, uses their own tools, may work for others, has no authority to bind Company, receives no employee benefits, holds and will keep every license and permit the services require, is responsible for their own taxes and insurance, and for any workers they use, including paying them, withholding taxes and carrying workers' compensation insurance where the law requires. Before the first payment Consultant will give Company a completed Form W-9. Company will report payments on Form 1099-NEC where the law requires.

{{#if workplaceFraud}}5. WORKPLACE FRAUD ACT NOTICE
The services are construction or landscaping services under Maryland's Workplace Fraud Act (Labor and Employment Article, Title 3, Subtitle 9). Consultant acknowledges that, when hired, Consultant received Company's written notice of Consultant's classification as an independent contractor, in English and Spanish, explaining what that classification means. Consultant acknowledges Consultant's duties to withhold, report and remit payroll taxes for all employees working for Consultant, to pay unemployment insurance taxes for all of them, and to maintain workers' compensation insurance. If Consultant is a business entity, Consultant will give Company on request a signed affidavit that it is an independent contractor available to work for other businesses, a current certificate of status from the Maryland State Department of Assessments and Taxation, and proof that it holds every occupational license the work requires.

{{/if}}6. WORK PRODUCT
Once Company pays for them, Consultant assigns to Company all rights in the deliverables created for Company under this Agreement, and will sign any further papers needed for this. Consultant keeps its own tools, methods, know-how and anything it had before or develops separately, and gives Company a non-exclusive license to use any of them that are built into the deliverables, for Company's own business. Consultant will not include another person's confidential information or protected material in the deliverables without permission.

6. NO GUARANTEE OF RESULTS
Consultant will give advice and services with professional care but does not guarantee any result. Company makes the final decisions about whether and how to use the advice.

{{#if confidential}}7. CONFIDENTIALITY
Consultant will keep Company's non-public information confidential, use it only for this work, and return or destroy it on request, during and after this Agreement. This does not cover information that is public through no fault of Consultant, was already known to Consultant, or must be disclosed by law. Nothing in this Agreement prevents Consultant from reporting a suspected violation of law to a government agency. Under the federal Defend Trade Secrets Act (18 U.S.C. §1833(b)), an individual is not criminally or civilly liable under any federal or state trade secret law for disclosing a trade secret (a) in confidence to a federal, state or local government official, either directly or indirectly, or to an attorney, solely to report or investigate a suspected violation of law, or (b) in a complaint or other document filed in a lawsuit or other proceeding, if the filing is made under seal. An individual who files a lawsuit for retaliation by an employer for reporting a suspected violation of law may disclose the trade secret to the individual's attorney and use it in the court case, if the individual files any document containing it under seal and does not disclose it except by court order.

{{/if}}{{#if limitLiability}}8. LIMIT OF LIABILITY
Consultant's total liability under this Agreement is limited to the fees Company paid for the services that gave rise to the claim, and neither party is liable to the other for indirect or consequential losses. This does not limit liability for fraud, willful misconduct or bodily injury, or any other liability that the law does not allow to be limited{{#if indemnity}}, or a party's duty to indemnify under the section on indemnity{{/if}}.

{{/if}}{{#if indemnity}}9. INDEMNITY
Each party will defend the other party against, and pay the losses from, a third party's claim to the extent the claim is caused by the first party's negligence, willful misconduct or breach of this Agreement. The party asking for protection must give prompt written notice of the claim and reasonable help, and the party giving protection controls the defense but may not settle in a way that binds the other party without its consent.

{{/if}}10. ENDING THE AGREEMENT
Either party may end this Agreement on 30 days' written notice, or sooner if the other materially breaks it and does not fix the problem within 15 days of written notice. When it ends, Company pays for services performed through the end date and, for a fixed fee, a fair share of the fee for the work done. Provisions that by their nature are meant to continue (such as those on payment, work product{{#if limitLiability}}{{#if confidential}}, limit of liability and confidentiality{{else}} and limit of liability{{/if}}{{else}}{{#if confidential}} and confidentiality{{/if}}{{/if}}) continue after this Agreement ends.

{{#if mediation}}11. DISPUTES
If a dispute arises, the parties will first try in good faith to settle it by talking, and then by mediation with a mediator they both accept, sharing the mediator's fee equally, before either starts a lawsuit. This does not prevent either party from asking a court for urgent protection of confidential information or ownership rights.

{{/if}}{{#if extraClauses}}12. ADDITIONAL TERMS
{{extraClauses}}

{{/if}}13. GENERAL
This is the parties' entire agreement, may be changed only in writing signed by both, and may not be assigned without the other party's written consent. Notices must be in writing and sent to the addresses above or to a new address given in writing. Delay in enforcing a right is not a waiver of it. If a term cannot be enforced, the rest stays in force. This Agreement may be signed in counterparts and electronically, and is governed by the laws of the State of {{state}}, whose courts may settle any dispute under it.

COMPANY: {{client}}
Signature: ______________________________   Date: ______________
Printed name: ______________________   Title (if a company): ______________

CONSULTANT: {{consultant}}
Signature: ______________________________   Date: ______________
Printed name: ______________________   Title (if a company): ______________`,
