    reviewNote: "CHECK FIRST (3 things): (1) Read the master lease: most forbid subletting without the landlord's written consent, and the use, term and rent here must fit it; attach a copy of it. (2) Get the landlord's consent page signed BEFORE the subtenant moves in. (3) The sublease ends when the master lease ends, so its end date must not be later than the master lease end date. ALSO FROM A REAL LEASE: if the master lease names two tenants (for example a company and its owner), enter the second in the \"another tenant\" box so both sign; the sublease gives the subtenant none of the tenant's renewal or purchase options; give the subtenant LESS time to cure than the master lease gives you; and this form is for business space only: a home needs the Residential Lease form with its sublease switch. DETAIL FOLLOWS. A sublease sits under the master lease: read the master lease first, because most commercial leases forbid subletting without the landlord's written consent and may limit the use, the term and the rent. This document includes a landlord consent page - get it signed before the subtenant moves in. The sublandlord stays responsible to the landlord for the master lease even after the sublease, and the sublease cannot outlast the master lease (this document says it ends when the master lease ends unless the landlord agrees in writing to keep the subtenant). Attach a copy of the master lease. Read from the statute text: Real Property Article 8-402(c) (written notice 60 days before a stated term ends or a month-to-month tenancy ends, 30 days from the tenant) covers every tenancy, not only homes, so the sublease promises the subtenant 60 days' written notice if the sublandlord wants the space back on the end date, and calendar that date; for a breach other than rent the sublandlord must give 30 days' written notice (14 for a clear and imminent danger) before asking the court to repossess (8-402.1), so the cure period is the longer of your number and 30 days; distress for rent (8-301 to 8-306) is a District Court action, not seizure by the sublandlord, and the sublease says possession and goods are taken only through the courts. Recording (3-101): if the sublease term, or any renewal term, is longer than seven years it is within the recording rule - sign a memorandum of sublease that every party signs (the sublease says so). A returned-payment fee is capped at $35 (Commercial Law 15-802). Written with Maryland in mind and compared with a standard commercial sublease form; these parts of that form were not copied because they are risky or unclear: ending all duties automatically when the master lease ends (this document ends the sublease but keeps money already owed), a mandatory loser-pays attorney's-fee rule (it is an option here), and re-entry by the landlord's own hands (this document says possession is retaken only through the courts). Rent for part of the premises is the same share of the master rent by floor area, there is holdover rent, and the landlord's consent page can confirm that the master lease is in force and no default is known (a landlord may strike it). Check the master lease for its own subletting rules and the subtenant's own tobacco, alcohol or lottery licenses (a sublease does not transfer a license), plus any local license. Whether to ask for a personal guarantee and the amount of the deposit are business choices. Companies must sign through an officer with a title.",
