    body: `NON-COMPETITION AND NON-SOLICITATION AGREEMENT

Date: {{effectiveDate}}

This agreement is between {{company}} ("Company") and {{person}}{{#if personAddress}} of {{personAddress}}{{/if}} (the "Person"). In exchange for {{#if relation=seller}}the purchase price Company paid for the business{{else}}employment or engagement by Company, pay and access to its confidential information{{#if consideration}} and {{consideration}}{{/if}}{{/if}}, the Person agrees as follows.{{#if alreadyEmployed}} The Person already works for Company and agrees that these promises are supported by {{#if consideration}}{{consideration}} and by {{/if}}Company's continuing to employ the Person.{{/if}}

1. NON-COMPETITION
{{#if relation=seller}}For {{months}} months after the sale of the business on {{saleDate}}, the Person will not, within {{miles}} miles of {{locationAddress}}, own (other than holding less than 2% of a public company), run, or work in a role similar to the Person's role for a business engaged in: {{activity}}.{{else}}{{#if !aboveLimit=yes}}This section does not apply to the Person: Maryland law (Md. Code, Lab. & Empl. § 3-716) does not allow a promise not to compete for a worker at this pay level. The sections below stay in force.{{else}}{{#if workerSector=healthlow}}This section does not apply to the Person: Maryland law (Md. Code, Lab. & Empl. § 3-716) does not allow a promise not to compete for this licensed health-care or veterinary worker. The sections below stay in force.{{else}}For {{months}} months after the Person's work for the Company ends for any reason, the Person will not, within {{miles}} miles of {{locationAddress}}, own (other than holding less than 2% of a public company), run, or work in a role similar to the Person's role for a business engaged in: {{activity}}. This section applies only if the Person earns more than 150% of the State minimum wage rate (Md. Code, Lab. & Empl. § 3-716) both when the Person signs this agreement and when the Person's work for the Company ends.{{#if workerSector=healthhigh}} In no event will this section last more than 1 year after the Person's last day of employment or reach more than 10 miles from the Person's primary place of employment, and on a patient's request the Company will tell the patient the new location where the Person will be practicing.{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}

{{#if customers}}2. CUSTOMERS AND SUPPLIERS
{{#if relation=seller}}For {{months}} months after the sale of the business on {{saleDate}}, the Person will not seek customers or suppliers of the business with whom the Person dealt, or about whom the Person learned confidential information, during the 12 months before the sale, to move their business away from the Company.{{else}}{{#if !aboveLimit=yes}}For {{months}} months after the Person's work for the Company ends for any reason, the Person will not use the Company's customer or supplier lists or other private customer or supplier information to seek those customers or suppliers to move their business away from the Company.{{else}}{{#if workerSector=healthlow}}For {{months}} months after the Person's work for the Company ends for any reason, the Person will not use the Company's customer or supplier lists or other private customer or supplier information to seek those customers or suppliers to move their business away from the Company.{{else}}For {{months}} months after the Person's work for the Company ends for any reason, the Person will not seek customers or suppliers of the Company with whom the Person dealt, or about whom the Person learned confidential information, during the last 12 months of the relationship, to move their business away from the Company.{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}

{{/if}}{{#if staff}}3. STAFF
{{#if relation=seller}}For {{months}} months after the sale of the business on {{saleDate}}, the Person will not hire, or encourage to leave, anyone who worked for the business during the 6 months before the sale.{{else}}{{#if !aboveLimit=yes}}For {{months}} months after the Person's work for the Company ends for any reason, the Person will not encourage anyone who worked for the Company during the last 6 months of the relationship to leave the Company.{{else}}{{#if workerSector=healthlow}}For {{months}} months after the Person's work for the Company ends for any reason, the Person will not encourage anyone who worked for the Company during the last 6 months of the relationship to leave the Company.{{else}}For {{months}} months after the Person's work for the Company ends for any reason, the Person will not hire, or encourage to leave, anyone who worked for the Company during the last 6 months of the relationship.{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}

{{/if}}{{#if confidential}}4. CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION
The Person will keep the Company's private business information (customer and supplier lists, prices, costs, financial records and methods) confidential and will not use it for anyone else, during and after the relationship. Nothing in this agreement stops the Person from reporting a possible violation of law to a government agency. Under 18 U.S.C. § 1833(b), an individual is not liable under any trade-secret law for disclosing a trade secret in confidence to a government official or an attorney solely to report or investigate a suspected violation of law, or in a sealed court filing.

{{/if}}5. FAIRNESS AND SEPARATE SECTIONS
The Person agrees the limits above are reasonable to protect the Company's legitimate business interests, and confirms the Person has had the chance to ask questions and to get advice from a lawyer of the Person's choice before signing. If a court finds any limit too broad, the parties ask the court to enforce it only to the extent it is reasonable. Each section stands on its own, and each time or distance limit is a separate promise: if one cannot be enforced, the others stay in force.

6. REMEDIES
If a party breaks this agreement the other may ask a court to order them to stop, in addition to any other remedy. The winning party recovers its reasonable costs of enforcing this agreement.

7. GENERAL
This is the whole agreement on this subject, may be changed only in writing signed by both, and is governed by the laws of the State of {{state}}. Company will give the Person a signed copy. The Company may assign this agreement to a successor to its business; the Person may not assign it. This agreement may be signed in copies, including electronically, and all copies together are one agreement.

{{#if additionalTerms}}8. ADDITIONAL TERMS
{{additionalTerms}}

{{/if}}COMPANY: {{company}}
Printed name and title: ______________________________
Signature: ______________________________   Date: ______________

PERSON: {{person}}
Signature: ______________________________   Date: ______________`,
